# Copy to .env.local (gitignored) and fill in. Every key here is optional — the app runs without
# any of them and says on screen what is switched off, rather than showing invented data.

# ── SERVER-ONLY. No EXPO_PUBLIC_ prefix: that prefix inlines the value into the client bundle,
#    and anything in the bundle is extractable from a shipped IPA. These are read by the routes
#    under src/app/api/ and never reach the device.

# Atlas chat. Free tier, no card required: https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
GEMINI_API_KEY=

# Search, quotes, charts, key stats, movers, branding logos, and news fallback.
# https://polygon.io  (free tier: 5 calls/min)
POLYGON_API_KEY=

# Options chains with greeks. The SANDBOX token is free and returns delayed quotes.
# https://developer.tradier.com
TRADIER_TOKEN=

# News with per-article sentiment. Falls back to Polygon news, then to "no stories right now".
# https://www.alphavantage.co/support/#api-key  (free tier: 25 calls/day)
ALPHAVANTAGE_API_KEY=

# ── CLIENT-SAFE. The EXPO_PUBLIC_ prefix is CORRECT here and nowhere else: the anon key is
#    designed to ship to clients and is protected by row-level security. Both are required
#    together — a URL with no key builds a client that fails every call.
#    Leave blank and auth stays off (src/lib/auth.ts, AUTH_ENABLED === false).
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# ── Production only. The deployed EAS Hosting origin. In development the app resolves the Metro
#    dev server automatically, so this stays blank.
EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=

# RevenueCat — the IAP SDK (Unit 5). EXPO_PUBLIC_ is CORRECT and not an oversight: a RevenueCat SDK
# key is a PUBLIC client key, like the Supabase anon key and unlike GEMINI_API_KEY. It identifies the
# app; it does not authorise anything an Apple receipt would not already prove.
#
# Without it, lib/purchases.ts configures nothing, IAP_ENABLED is false, and the paywall renders its
# purchase control disabled WITH ITS REASON ON SCREEN rather than silently inert.
#
# Also required before a purchase can complete, and neither is in this file:
#   - App Store Connect products `euphoria_pro_monthly` ($9.99) and `euphoria_pro_yearly` ($79.99),
#     attached to the CURRENT offering in the RevenueCat dashboard
#   - a RevenueCat entitlement whose identifier is exactly `pro`
#   - a sandbox tester account, and a Configuration.storekit file for simulator runs (UI flow only,
#     never real billing)
EXPO_PUBLIC_REVENUECAT_IOS_KEY=
